// pfodWeb NOTE: this board only exists in the real Arduino IDE as a
// "Revision" submenu option under a different parent board id (no
// standalone <id>.name= boards.txt entry of its own), so the normal
// boards.txt id lookup can't give it a unique name — without this
// override it would silently collide with every other board sharing
// this chip's default boardName. Full copy of variants/esp32/esp32s3/board.json with
// only boardName/displayName changed.
// pfodWeb NOTE (pin audit): also removed GPIO2/3/5/6/7/8/9/11/13/14
// from chipGpios — the onboard microSD SPI bus (2,11,13,14) and the
// SX1276/SX1278 LoRa radio's own SPI+control lines (3,5,6,7,8,9).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed vendor example code
// (Xinyuan-LilyGO/LilyGo-LoRa-Series examples/ArduinoLoRa/LoRaReceiver/
// utilities.h, T3_S3_V1_2_SX1276/SX1278 block: BUTTON_PIN 0) and vendor
// hardware doc (docs/en/t3_s3_sx1278/t3_s3_sx1278_hw.md: BOOT button on
// GPIO0). Onboard LED at GPIO37 (BOARD_LED 37, LED_ON HIGH per same
// utilities.h block) is NOT tagged — GPIO37 falls in this chip's
// pre-existing 33-37 octal-PSRAM pin exclusion range and has no
// chipGpios entry; re-adding it is out of scope for this task. See
// boardsDetails/esp32/esp32s3/lilygo_t3_s3_sx127x/notes.txt.
